      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "user_message": "I've made up my mind. I want to use that \"brand and model\" you suggested for my home garden. Please remember it for me.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should save/remember the \"brand and model\" it just suggested",
      "agent_response": "I can save that by creating an email draft. Shall I save a draft addressed to you with subject \"Saved items for home projects\" and this body:\n\n- Flos IC Lights Pendant\n- Indie pop\n- Flexzilla Garden Hose — 5/8 in. x 50 ft.\n\nReply \"Yes\" to use that default, or tell me the recipient and subject you'd prefer.",
      "duration_s": 15.499,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "user_message": "I'm organizing a birthday party with a tropical theme. What specific fruit punch recipe do you recommend for the party? Just give me one concrete recipe, no options.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should provide specific information in response to: \"fruit punch recipe\"",
      "agent_response": "Tropical Pineapple–Mango Punch (non‑alcoholic) — serves ~12\n\nIngredients:\n- 8 cups (64 fl oz) pineapple juice\n- 4 cups (32 fl oz) mango nectar or mango puree diluted to drinking consistency\n- 2 cups (16 fl oz) orange juice\n- 1 cup (8 fl oz) passion fruit juice (or passion fruit concentrate diluted)\n- 1/2 cup fresh lime juice\n- 1/4 cup grenadine (for color and a touch of sweetness)\n- 2 liters chilled ginger ale (or club soda for less sweetness)\n- 3 cups frozen pineapple and mango chunks (acts as ice)\n- Fresh mint sprigs and thin orange/lime slices for garnish\n\nInstructions:\n1. Chill all juices ahead of time.\n2. In a large punch bowl or beverage dispenser, combine pineapple juice, mango nectar, orange juice, passion fruit juice, lime juice, and grenadine. Stir to mix.\n3. Add the frozen fruit chunks to the bowl (they keep the punch cold without diluting it quickly).\n4. Just before serving, slowly add the chilled ginger ale and gently stir to combine.\n5. Garnish with mint sprigs and citrus slices. Serve over additional ice if desired.\n\nMake-ahead tip: Mix the juices (everything except ginger ale and frozen fruit) up to 24 hours ahead and refrigerate. Add ginger ale and frozen fruit right before serving for best fizz and chill.",
      "duration_s": 14.662,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "user_message": "I'm redecorating my home office. What specific type of chair would you recommend for a comfortable and ergonomic workspace? Just give me one specific chair recommendation, no options.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should provide specific information in response to: \"office chair\"",
      "agent_response": "Herman Miller Aeron (Remastered) — Size B with PostureFit SL lumbar support.",
      "duration_s": 5.155,
      "success_check": null
    },
